  "summary": {
    "key_findings": [
      "Australia non-competitive rate (53.3%) is 1.8x the EU average (~30%), confirming dead-zone vulnerability extends beyond Europe.",
      "Across 8 major non-EU economies, estimated EUR 679bn in annual procurement occurs in competitive dead zones.",
      "Combined with EU dead-zone exposure (~EUR 260bn from paper), global dead-zone procurement exceeds EUR 900bn annually.",
      "High-emission sectors (Manufacturing, Energy, Transport) are also major procurement sectors, amplifying carbon intensity risks.",
      "Sector variation is dramatic: Industrial/Manufacturing SB rate (91.4%) vs Professional Services (40.0%) in Australia.",
      "Construction has low direct emissions but high scope-3 exposure, making procurement competition in this sector critical for embodied carbon."
    ]
  }
